 ### [Volume Shading Modes](1550-volume-shading-modes.md)
 Volume Shading Modes are a set of three shading strategies applied during volume ray marching to compute lighting and shadows for each sample along a ray. They extend the Phong Shading Model for Volume Data by providing specific heuristics for handling illumination in participating media, distinguishing themselves through their approach to gradient estimation and shadow accumulation.
+
+### Phong Shading (Gradient Shader)
+A shading technique that modulates intensity by the strength of the local gradient raised to a power, similar to Phong shading in polygon rendering [S4]. It calculates the absolute value of the derivative (1D gradient) of the input signal, raises the gradient magnitude to a power to accentuate regions of rapid change, and multiplies the original input signal by the raised gradient result to select regions of rapid change [S4]. The exponent controls highlight width, where higher powers narrow the highlight and introduce more high frequencies [S4]. The gradient operator acts as a high-pass filter (Fourier transform $j\omega$) that enhances high frequencies, which can cause aliasing during resampling if not filtered [S4].
 
